+
+## Addendum — closure check r4 (`reviews/M1-C1.1-r4-closure.md`, merged as `7ba98f1`)
+
+Fixes: `6c290ad`. **No reviewer-owned test file was edited this round.** `git diff` of every reviewer test
+location (`crates/*/tests`, `desktop/src/ipc/c11-r*`, `desktop/src/test`, `tests/`) against the merge is empty. Both
+new regressions in `crates/model/tests/c11_r4_exposure_bounds.rs` pass unchanged.
+
+### C11-R4-01 — exposure bounds at the patch boundary — **fixed** (`6c290ad`)
+
+Every frame-bearing write is bounded by the scene-length limit (10 §5, 100 000 frames) **before** anything is expanded,
+resized or applied. A breach is `doc.limitExceeded`, with `details.pointer` set to the operation's path and
+`details.maxFrames`; the input is untouched.
+
+- **Run parsing** — `change.rs:387` `parse_runs`. Counts must be ≥ 1, and the total is computed arithmetically
+  (saturating) and must not exceed 100 000. `expand_runs` uses it, so nothing larger than a scene is ever allocated
+  (the old `2 × MAX` post-expansion bound is gone).
+- **Exposure range replace** — `change.rs:682`, `:729`. The checks run in this order:
+  1. the window's `from`/`to` must lie within frame 100 000 (the reviewer's one-frame distant window);
+  2. the run totals of the target, `value` and `oldValue` (`runs_total`, `:426`);
+  3. the `to`-consistency;
+  4. the resulting length, `max(target, window end) − |old| + |new|`.
+- **Mouth-track range replace** — `change.rs:682`, `:713`. The same window check, plus the resulting string length.
+- **Whole-value `add`/`replace` of a declared `exposure`** — `change.rs:773`. Same counts and total. Lookalikes inside
+  `meta`/`ext` are not run-bearing fields (`declared_frame_field`, `:440`, consistent with C11-R3-01).
+- The integrity check (`validate.rs:849`, total ≤ 100 000; `runCount`) is unchanged and still applies.
+
+Limit and over-limit cases for every run-bearing write are in the unit test
+`frame_bearing_writes_are_bounded_at_the_scene_limit` (`change.rs:946`). It covers:
+- an exposure range value of 100 000 frames (accepted) and of 100 001 (rejected);
+- a one-frame window at frame 100 000 (accepted) and at 100 001 (rejected);
+- a full 100 000-frame exposure lengthened by zero frames (accepted) and by one (rejected);
+- an oversized `oldValue` and target (`u32::MAX` frames), refused before expansion;
+- whole-value `replace` and `add` of 100 000 frames (accepted) and 100 001 (rejected), plus a zero count;
+- an opaque `meta.exposure` lookalike, which is not a run-bearing field and is not bounded;
+- a mouth-track value of 100 000 letters (accepted) and 100 001 (rejected), a window at frame 100 000 (accepted) and
+  one past it (rejected), and a full 100 000-letter track lengthened by one (rejected).
+
+Exactly 100 000 frames stays valid everywhere.
+
+**Register row 388** (10 §2.6, change sets/inversion/ranges): implemented. Sources `change.rs:387, :426, :682,
+:729, :773`; tests `c11_r4_exposure_bounds.rs::exposure_range_rejects_total_above_scene_limit`,
+`::exposure_range_rejects_window_past_scene_limit`, the unit test above, and the round-3 inversion and zero-count
+tests.
+
+### CI omission — **fixed** (`6c290ad`)
+
+- A new step, **"Reviewer Python suites (every tests/adversarial/*.py)"**, runs in `check (windows-latest)` and
+  `check (macos-latest)` and calls `scripts/run-reviewer-python-suites.py`.
+- The runner discovers every `tests/adversarial/*.py` (11 suites today), runs each in isolated mode from the
+  repository root, and fails if any fails. It excludes only `collect_runtime_evidence.py`, named with its reason: an
+  M0 evidence collector, not a test.
+- `c04-r3-page.py` starts Vitest through `cmd /c`, which exists only on Windows. On macOS the runner performs the
+  same copy, run and delete itself, so the reviewer file is unchanged. The shim was also exercised locally.
+- The check jobs now check out full history (`fetch-depth: 0`), because the policy suite diffs against `0460ad0`.
+- The handoff lists the CI job and step that run every reviewer suite: Rust, Vitest, Python and `guards.mjs`.
+
+### Gates
+
+Raw logs are in `reviews/evidence/M1-C1.1-r4-response/gates/`, with hashes in `receipt.json`:
+- fmt; clippy and the diagnostics clippy;
+- `cargo test --workspace --locked`: **281 passed**, 1 standing ignore;
+- diagnostics tests and `cargo deny`;
+- `pnpm` lint, typecheck, test (**Vitest 39 files / 326 passed; Node 9**), format and licences;
+- both front-end builds (dist check ok);
+- headless build, selftest ×2 and the dependency guard;
+- **reviewer Python suites 11/11**.
+
+CI: run **39179514794** on `07f992d`, all 8 jobs green; its "Reviewer Python suites" step passed 11/11 on both Windows
+and macOS.
